Third-party software
--------------------
The Windows installer bundles the following programs unmodified, each under
its own license:

* FFmpeg (ffmpeg.exe) — an LGPL build from BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds, licensed under
  the GNU Lesser General Public License; its license text ships next to it as
  ffmpeg-LICENSE.txt. Source code: https://ffmpeg.org/ and
  https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds.
* uv (uv.exe) by Astral — dual-licensed under Apache-2.0 or MIT; both texts
  ship next to it as uv-LICENSE.txt. https://github.com/astral-sh/uv

The experimental macOS build (Apple Silicon) bundles uv (same terms) and
FFmpeg built from the unmodified FFmpeg 8.1.3 source release
(https://ffmpeg.org/releases/) in an LGPL configuration (no GPL or non-free
components), statically linked with the Opus codec 1.6.1 (BSD license,
Copyright Xiph.Org Foundation and contributors, https://opus-codec.org/). The
LGPL text, the Opus license and the exact build configuration ship next to it
as ffmpeg-LICENSE.txt; scripts/build_release_macos.sh reproduces the build.
It also bundles meet-audiotap, a helper of this project (Apache-2.0) for
system audio capture.

The application window bundles the Onest typeface (variable font, Cyrillic
and Latin), Copyright 2021 The Onest Project Authors
(https://github.com/simpals/onest), licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1; it is taken from the @fontsource-variable/onest package.
Interface icons come from Lucide (lucide-react), Copyright Lucide Icons and
Contributors, licensed under the ISC License (https://lucide.dev).

JavaScript and Rust libraries compiled into the application window and shell
(React, Tauri, xterm.js and others) keep their own licenses, listed in
app/package-lock.json and app/src-tauri/Cargo.lock.

Python packages (faster-whisper, CTranslate2, pyannote.audio, PyTorch,
transformers, GigaAM and others) are installed from their package indexes on
first run under their own licenses; they are not part of this repository.
GigaAM (https://github.com/salute-developers/GigaAM; MIT License, Copyright
(c) 2024 GigaChat Team) is installed from a pinned commit of its GitHub
repository.

Models
------
Models are downloaded at runtime (from Hugging Face; GigaAM — from its
authors' server) and are not distributed with this product; each is governed
by its own license:

* Speech recognition (GPU profile): bzikst/faster-whisper-large-v3-russian —
  a CTranslate2 conversion of antony66/whisper-large-v3-russian (a Russian
  fine-tune of OpenAI Whisper large-v3); Apache-2.0.
* Speech recognition (CPU profile, default): GigaAM v3 (v3_e2e_rnnt, and
  v3_e2e_ctc on request) by GigaChat Team — downloaded from the GigaAM authors'
  server into the application's models folder; MIT.
* Speech recognition (CPU profile, Whisper option): Systran/faster-whisper-medium —
  OpenAI Whisper medium in CTranslate2 format; MIT.
  (faster-whisper and CTranslate2 themselves are MIT-licensed.)
* Word timestamps (forced alignment):
  jonatasgrosman/wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53-russian — wav2vec2 XLSR-53
  fine-tuned for Russian; Apache-2.0.
* Speaker diarization and voice embeddings:
  pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1 — CC-BY-4.0 (pyannote.audio code
  is MIT-licensed); requires accepting its terms of use on Hugging Face
  before download.

